This software is a reference overlay services host: it assembles the
released BSV overlay engine as a library, stores through that engine's own
storage, and takes a multicast delivery fabric as its transport. Objects
delivered by the fabric reach it as ordinary BRC-22 submissions from the
bridge beside it, and its chain tracker is that bridge's block-header
store, so every object it admits is verified against headers the host
itself received. The engine is not modified and not forked, and the host's
own propagation is switched off by holding no advertiser: the fabric is
the propagation.

